From d229c79e38d128a29accad5deebfb13cdec11475 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cozima <cozima0210@yahoo.co.jp>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:53:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(s3): apply bucket CORS to virtual-hosted-style requests
 (#8860)

ConditionalCorsLayer took the bucket from the first path segment only.
With RUSTFS_SERVER_DOMAINS set, a virtual-hosted-style request such as
OPTIONS http://mybucket.localhost:9000/x.jpg was evaluated against a
bucket named "x.jpg", so a preflight never matched the bucket's CORS
configuration and returned 200 without Access-Control-* headers, while
the same request in path style succeeded.

Resolve the bucket from the host prefix first, reusing the virtual-host
matching that the API rate limiter already uses, and fall back to the
first path segment for path-style requests. A bucket-level request on a
virtual host ("/") is now treated as a bucket request instead of the
server root.

Co-authored-by: cozima <8464261+cozima@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
